        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'US war on Iran not about the Iranian people: Europe can put the issue of human rights on the table' Middle East Issued on: 03/06/2026 - 17:24 Modified: 03/06/2026 - 17:52 Nadia Massih is pleased to welcome Mahmood Amiry-Moghaddam, President of Iran Human Rights and Professor of Neuroscience at University of Oslo. He offers a stark assessment of the Iranian regime's response to recent unrest and wartime conditions. Professor Amiry-Moghaddam argues that the authorities have exploited international attention on regional conflict to intensify domestic repression. Civilians are effectively \"risking their lives\" so that \"the world can know what is happening in Iran,\" underscoring both the scale of repression and the resilience of civil society under authoritarian rule. 'Palestinians are unbelievable people: Vast majority of in Gaza just want to live a normal life' 03/06/2026 Middle East Israel and Hezbollah exchange fire amid new talks in Washington 03/06/2026 Middle East Trump denies impasse in Iran talks after fresh strikes on Gulf countries 03/06/2026 Middle East Israel strikes hospital in southern Lebanon 03/06/2026 Middle East New round of Israel-Lebanon talks opens after Israeli strikes 03/06/2026 Middle East Kuwait airport hit by Iranian drones as US and Iran trade fire 03/06/2026 Middle East Trump's acknowledgment of Hezbollah 'utterly humiliating' for Netanyahu 02/06/2026 Middle East 'Healthy consensus in Israel' on pursuing Lebanon campaign, expert says 01/06/2026 Middle East 'Most extreme right-wing fringes of Netanyahu govt call for far greater military action in Lebanon' 01/06/2026 Middle East"
